   "daf": "14b",
   "sentenceId": 17,
   "he": "וּמְסַלֵּק אֶת לְבוֹנָתָהּ לְצַד אֶחָד. כִּי הֵיכִי דְּלָא תִּקְּמוֹץ בַּהֲדֵי מִנְחָה, כְּדִתְנַן: קָמַץ וְעָלָה בְּיָדוֹ צְרוֹר אוֹ גַּרְגֵּר מֶלַח אוֹ קוֹרֶט לְבוֹנָה — פָּסוּל.",
   "en": "The baraita states: «And he removes its frankincense to one side.» The Gemara explains: This is done «in order that» the frankincense «not be removed along with the meal-offering» when the priest removes a handful. «As we learned» in a mishna (Menaḥot 6a): If he «removed» the «handful and a pebble, or a grain of salt, or a crumb [koret] of frankincense came out in his hand, it is invalid.» The handful must be entirely fine flour."
  }
 ],
